Here is an example TPM key pair and also an MOK key pair.

The TPM key pair is generated with .aux/generate-tpm-keys and the MOK
key pair is generated with .aux/generate-mok.

It is not normal to have the private keys made public as is done here.
Thus, systems built with these keys do not provide much actual security.
However, while we use our own private keys for actual production systems,
we are making these keys public so that their functionality can be tested
by anyone.  As Puavo OS is a public project, it is fair that anyone can
use these keys to create an actual Puavo OS system.

However, you should know that in case you actually want to use SecureBoot
and TPM to achieve some security, you should roll out your own keys and
keep the private keys secret.
